  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "SiNqPIhXWrrjhIhTvtHG5GregMQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:49.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "`@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-graphql` is server-agnostic \u2014 it ships `typedefs`, `AnalyticsResolvers`, `AnalyticsModel` and the `queryFilter` type, and nothing else. The piece that is easy to miss is that the resolvers are not self-sufficient: they read an `AnalyticsModel` off the request context at the exact path `dataSources.db.Analytics`. Wire the schema without it and the resolvers fail at request time, not at boot.\n\n`AnalyticsModel` is the adapter that connects GraphQL types to a store, and it wraps an `AnalyticsQueryEngine`, which in turn wraps an `IAnalyticsStore`:\n\n```typescript\nconst model = new AnalyticsModel(\n  new AnalyticsQueryEngine(store),   // store: any IAnalyticsStore\n);\n```\n\nWith Apollo 4 the context factory is where it goes \u2014 note this is the express middleware's context, not the `ApolloServer` constructor:\n\n```typescript\nconst schema = makeExecutableSchema({ typeDefs: typedefs, resolvers: AnalyticsResolvers });\nconst server = new ApolloServer({ schema, plugins });\nawait server.start();\n\napp.use(\"/graphql\", express.json(), expressMiddleware(server, {\n  context: ({ req }) => ({\n    dataSources: { db: { Analytics: model } },   // required by the resolvers\n  }),\n}));\n```\n\nThe in-repo reference implementation is `packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/analytics-subgraph.ts`, and it is worth reading before hand-rolling the express version: `AnalyticsSubgraph` takes the `IAnalyticsStore` off its `SubgraphArgs`, constructs `new AnalyticsModel(new AnalyticsQueryEngine(store))`, and then injects the context through `graphqlManager.setAdditionalContextFields({ dataSources: { db: { Analytics: model } } })` rather than through a per-request context callback. Same required path, supplied once at subgraph construction.\n\nThe library is documented as tested against Apollo Server 3 and 4; a fuller worked example lives in the MakerDAO-SES ecosystem-api repository.\n\nChoosing the store: the academy snippet constructs the engine over `MemoryAnalyticsStore` imported from `@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-browser`. That class does not exist anywhere in the monorepo \u2014 `git grep MemoryAnalyticsStore` returns zero hits outside the academy docs \u2014 so the snippet cannot compile as written. Substitute `PostgresAnalyticsStore` from `@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-pg` for a Node/server process (this is what `reactor-api` itself does, even locally, where its `knex` handle is backed by PGlite), or `BrowserAnalyticsStore` from `@powerhousedao/analytics-engine-browser` when the engine runs in a browser. Any `IAnalyticsStore` satisfies `AnalyticsQueryEngine`, so the resolver wiring above is unchanged either way.\n\nProvenance: draft `03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/graphql/integration.md`, whose store import is stale. `AnalyticsModel`, `AnalyticsResolvers` and `schema.ts` confirmed present in `packages/analytics-engine/graphql/src/`; the `dataSources.db.Analytics` path confirmed at `AnalyticsResolvers.ts` lines 11, 54 and 77; the subgraph wiring confirmed in `packages/reactor-api/src/graphql/analytics-subgraph.ts` at 6.2.2-dev.45.\n\n_Source-verified 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse source at v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:34:49.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:34:49.000Z"
    }
  },
